      "message": "In this CL, the speed feature `disable_loop_restoration_luma` is replaced with `disable_sgr_filter` and `disable_wiener_coeff_refine_search`.\n\nThe speed feature `disable_loop_restoration_luma` disables the loop restoration only for the luma component, whereas `disable_sgr_filter` and `disable_wiener_coeff_refine_search` apply for both luma and chroma. As `disable_loop_restoration_chroma` is already enabled for speed \u003e\u003d 3, we have used the existing speed features `disable_sgr_filter` and `disable_wiener_coeff_refine_search` to disable for luma.\nAnother approach would be to introduce new speed features such as `disable_sgr_filter_luma` and `disable_wiener_coeff_refine_search_luma` that will work only for luma. This approach improves the readability of speed feature settings. Please let us know your opinion.\n\n Performance results of encoder and decoder are as follows:\n \n ```\n                        Instruction\n                     Count Reduction(%)          BD-Rate Loss (%)            \ncpu    Resolution    Encoder  Decoder   avg.psnr  ovr.psnr   ssim    vmaf    vmaf_neg\n 4     LOWRES2       -0.072   -0.344    -0.0257   -0.0243   0.0218  -0.2007  -0.1992\n 4     MIDRES2       -0.121   -0.207    -0.0972   -0.0853  -0.0248  -0.2980  -0.2302\n 4     SHORTS608P    -0.145   -0.338    -0.0506   -0.0576  -0.0702  -0.2288  -0.1455\n 4     SHORTS720P    -0.163   -0.258    -0.0207   -0.0305  -0.0183  -0.1932  -0.0963\n 4     SHORTS1080P   -0.104   -0.171    -0.0423   -0.0287  -0.0028  -0.1101  -0.0519\n 4     HDRES2        -0.115   -0.488    -0.0755   -0.0841  -0.0598  -0.4995  -0.3505\n 4     Average       -0.121   -0.297    -0.0507   -0.0506  -0.0261  -0.2480  -0.1716\n \n 5     LOWRES2       -0.268   -0.304    -0.0437   -0.0447  -0.0292  -0.4296  -0.3202\n 5     MIDRES2       -0.300   -0.424    -0.1161   -0.1196  -0.0901  -0.2784  -0.2565\n 5     SHORTS608P    -0.244   -0.296     0.0524    0.0255   0.0144  -0.0144   0.0157\n 5     SHORTS